## Phase 3.1: Render targets and depth
Docs: [Resource System](../planning/subsystems/resource-system.md), [Command Model](../planning/subsystems/command-model.md), [Resource State Model](../planning/subsystems/resource-state-model.md)
- [ ] Implement render target textures and views.
- [ ] Implement depth/stencil textures and views.
- [ ] Define load/store and clear semantics for render targets.
- [ ] Implement resolve commands and render-target blits using the shared copy/blit surface.

## Phase 3.2: Render pass and framebuffer mapping
Docs: [Resource State Model](../planning/subsystems/resource-state-model.md), [Driver Backends](../planning/subsystems/driver-backends.md), [Resource System](../planning/subsystems/resource-system.md), [Command Model](../planning/subsystems/command-model.md)
- [ ] Define framebuffer or render pass descriptors in the RHI.
- [ ] Implement begin/end render pass command surface in the command context.
- [ ] Map render pass state to OpenGL framebuffers.
- [ ] Record attachment access intent for render passes (full validation in Phase 4).

## Phase 3.3: Presentation path
Docs: [Presentation](../planning/subsystems/presentation.md), [Synchronization](../planning/subsystems/synchronization.md), [Command Model](../planning/subsystems/command-model.md)
- [ ] Implement swapchain/viewport creation using platform surface contract.
- [ ] Implement present scheduling and vsync selection.
- [ ] Handle resize, color space, and present mode selection.
- [ ] Support multi-window and headless swapchain creation paths.
- [ ] Integrate acquire/present synchronization with the submit boundary.
- [ ] Define buffering defaults and zero-size/minimized surface behavior.
